{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/493476-central-europe-the-night-wolves-pack-ride-across-poland","id":493476,"title":"[Central Europe] The 'Night Wolves' Pack ride across Poland","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T05:20:53-07:00","id":493476,"title":"[Central Europe] The 'Night Wolves' Pack ride across Poland","content":"Today, <a href=\"http://www.france24.com/en/20150426-russia-night-wolves-bikers-vow-ride-berlin-despite-bans-zaldostanov/\" target=\"_blank\">Poland is all about the <i>Night Wolves</i> pro-Putin bikers riding across our country to the Berlin</a>. We are prepared for some internationalist incidents in the way of they ride, especially as our Prime Minister Ewa Kopacz banned they entering our country.<br /> <br /> Listening about it it struck me the feeling of &quot;violation of mine territory&quot; - probably the same way Uratha feel when their enemies are on their turf. So here is topic idea - how could you see this event in<b> Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> setting?<br /> <br /> <i>Night Wolves</i> bikers sounds as 2ed Pack, with some inner circle having they own agenda, and most of members being just mortal or maybe few Wolf-Blooded. They want to get to Berlin - but why? Maybe they use the ride as occasion to test Polish Uratha and look for weak spots in defense of territory? Maybe they look for something in Wroc\u0142aw hunting grounds?<br /> <br /> And most important - what Tribe they would be? Ultranationalist sound to me as Ivory Claws, but I could also see Storm Lords or Blood Talons as them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:08:42-07:00","id":496354,"title":"","content":"I'd say that maybe they are hunting something which ran away, or came from, Berlin? As for tribe I'd love to put them as Predator Kings but I know that I'll have to put them as Blood Talons or Ivory Claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:13:00-07:00","id":496404,"title":"","content":"It could be a mixture of tribes. Nationalism usually tries to hearken back to a better time, so I'd probably stick them with the Pure, though. In my first werewolf game we were next door to a pack of Fire-Touched. And they would occasionally skirt the edge of our territory antagonistically, just pissing on walls and stuff that seemed strange because appearance wise they seemed like very uptight, prudish religious folks. They even had a church, which was their base of operations. And we never really did anything about it until the end because they outnumbered us at least four to one.<br /> <br /> So they knew we wouldn't start something by attacking them, but they tried to get us to anyways, just encroaching on our territory like I mentioned. It could be something as simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}